      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Both ACE inhibitors and ARBs are Class I first-line choices for high blood pressure, but ARBs are often preferred first due to fewer side effects.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "ARBs are often preferred first due to fewer side effects"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Guideline overview:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Major guidelines (ACC/AHA, ESC/ESH) give both classes equal Class I, Level A recommendations for starting therapy."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Head-to-room/observational and review data show similar blood pressure reduction and heart/kidney protection ."
          }
        ]
      },
